{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "inbound/a-headless-turn-s-provider-error-reaches-the-caller-and-on-error",
  "title": "A turn whose provider fails, in a room with no streaming target, returns the error to the caller and fires ON_ERROR once, named ProviderError; a failure of another kind reaches the caller too",
  "rules": [
    "§10.1 step 18",
    "§9.2",
    "§12.2 step 13s"
  ],
  "setup": {
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "sms1",
        "type": "sms",
        "category": "transport"
      },
      {
        "id": "streamed",
        "type": "ai",
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "refuses": {
                "status": 503,
                "message": "connection error"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "other",
        "type": "ai",
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "fails": "unexpected boom"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "rooms": [
      {
        "id": "room-1",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "sms1"
          },
          {
            "channel_id": "streamed",
            "category": "intelligence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "room-2",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "sms1"
          },
          {
            "channel_id": "other",
            "category": "intelligence"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "hooks": [
      {
        "name": "errors",
        "trigger": "on_error",
        "execution": "async"
      }
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "call": "process_inbound",
      "room_id": "room-1",
      "message": {
        "channel_id": "sms1",
        "sender_id": "u1",
        "content": {
          "type": "text",
          "body": "go"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": {
          "blocked": false,
          "error": {
            "$contains": "connection error"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "idle": true
    },
    {
      "call": "process_inbound",
      "room_id": "room-2",
      "message": {
        "channel_id": "sms1",
        "sender_id": "u1",
        "content": {
          "type": "text",
          "body": "go"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": {
          "blocked": false,
          "error": {
            "$contains": "unexpected boom"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "idle": true
    }
  ],
  "expect": {
    "hooks": {
      "errors": [
        {
          "trigger": "on_error",
          "room_id": "room-1",
          "event": {
            "source": {
              "channel_id": "streamed",
              "channel_type": "ai"
            },
            "metadata": {
              "error_type": "ProviderError",
              "error": {
                "$contains": "connection error"
              },
              "error_category": "streaming"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "trigger": "on_error",
          "room_id": "room-2",
          "event": {
            "source": {
              "channel_id": "other",
              "channel_type": "ai"
            },
            "metadata": {
              "error": {
                "$contains": "unexpected boom"
              },
              "error_category": "streaming"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "notes": "Python: tests/test_inbound_stream_error_propagation.py::test_provider_error_propagates_and_still_fires_on_error (room-1) and test_non_provider_error_also_propagates (room-2). The only transport is the source: the stream is read with no target, and its failure is the caller's as it is ON_ERROR's. Python's non-streaming twins (test_non_streaming_provider_error_propagates_with_cause, test_non_streaming_provider_error_fires_on_error) fail in its provider's generate(), which a scripted round read whole does not reach: a runner ignores fails and refuses on a whole_response round. Not compared: the error's cause, which Python's test reads on its exception (a ConnectionError under the ProviderError)."
}
